  "query_preview": "..\nIssued Issued 1200 AM CDT Fri Sep 10 2026\n\nSunday through Thursday:\n\nHigh pressure returns to the region for Sunday resulting is a \npleasant seasonal end to the weekend with highs only in the 70s \nand lows dipping into the 50s and maybe even cracking into the \nupper 40s. This high pressure is not expected to hang around for\ntoo long and quickly shifts east overnight Sunday into Monday \nas the pattern becomes a bit more active for the start of the \nweek. Upstream a trough is progged to lift across the Northern \nRockies and Northern Plains through the day. Ahead of it, \nlooking at low-level WAA to gradually increase along with \nsoutherly surface winds and moisture advection to lift into \nsouthern WI during this time. Models continue to favor increased\nPoP chances (+40%) along the low-level WAA and surface warm \nfront overnight Sunday through the day on Monday. Then later \nMonday night into early Tuesday expect the cold front to swing \nthrough the region as the main low traverses across the James \nBay region. \n\nWhile, this places southern WI in the warm sector of this \nsystem, a bulk of the latest mid-range guidances is keeping the \nupper-level dynamics to our north. Meanwhile any convection will\nbe driven by low-level WAA, and unseasonable stronger LLJ, and \ntiming of the cold frontal passage, which this far out is tough \nto pinpoint exact details. Also given the trend for more midday \nprecip chances, may end up limiting instability building into \nsouthern WI and paired with later overnight/early morning timing\nof the cold front across our neck of the woods, may ultimately \nlimit our thunderstorm potential with this early week system. \nNevertheless, still plenty of time for things to shift and if we\nsee this system slow down and the 40-50 kt LLJ scenarios \nmaterialize, it may be enough for a few stronger storms and \npotentially minor flooding concerns for portions of southern \nWI. Will continue to monitor over the coming days, but it does \nbear watching.\n\nBehind the start of the week system, things are progged to \nsettle down a bit toward the middle of next week as high \npressure is progged to filter in behind it and bring a cooler \nairmass to the area.\n\nWagner",
